@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# ADR-001: Store recipients as a copied `sharedWith` array on the note
+
+- Status: proposed
+- Change: share-note-with-colleague
+- Date: 2026-10-06
+
+## Context
+REQ-note-sharing-001 returns the note with its `sharedWith` list. `NotesRepo` returns shallow copies (`{ ...note }`), so a nested array would alias stored state and let any caller mutate recipients outside the authorization path.
+
+## Decision
+Each note gets `sharedWith: string[]` (initialized `[]` in `create`). `NotesRepo.share(id, userId)` adds the id only if absent and returns a copy. Every repo return clones `sharedWith` as well as the note.
+
+## Alternatives
+- Separate `Map<noteId, Set<userId>>` in the repo: needs a join on every read and on the response body; no benefit in memory.
+- `Set` on the note: not JSON-serializable as the response body.
+
+## Consequences
+All note bodies gain an additive `sharedWith` field. Idempotency is local to the repo. Easily reversible: no persistence or migration.
