@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# ADR-002: Separate tenant-scoped read predicate from owner-only write predicate
+
+- Status: proposed
+- Change: share-note-with-colleague
+- Date: 2026-10-06
+
+## Context
+Sharing grants read access only (REQ-note-sharing-006/007). Reusing one access check for all methods would give recipients write access; the config requires tenant context in every authorization check.
+
+## Decision
+`src/app.js` uses `canRead(note, user)` = same tenant AND (owner OR in `sharedWith`) for `GET /notes` and `GET /notes/:id`, and `isOwner(note, user)` = same tenant AND owner for `PUT`, `DELETE`, and `POST /notes/:id/share`. The tenant clause is evaluated first in both, and the existing 404 for other-tenant notes runs before either.
+
+## Alternatives
+- Single "can access" predicate: leaks write access to recipients.
+- Inline checks per route: list and detail visibility could diverge.
+
+## Consequences
+List and detail visibility stay consistent; future read-only grants extend only `canRead`. Recipient writes are rejected with 403. Easily reversible.
